-Java Naming Conventions (Java coding conventions):
---------------------------------------------------
-Java language followed some standards for pre-defined packages,classes and methods
-Java language suggested java programmers also to follow same standards
-Following these standards is not mandatory but highly recommended (Optional but recommended)
1. Naming conventions for the Class name:
----------------------------------------
A class name can contain any number of words without spaces.
Recommended to write every word first letter as uppercase
2. Naming conventions for the variable name:
--------------------------------------------
A variable name can contain any number of words without spaces.
Recommended to start word first letter as lowercase
If variable name contains multiple words then recommended to write from second word onwords every first character in Uppercase
eg: int age; int userAge; long creaditCardNumber;
3. Naming conventions for the method name:
-----------------------------------------
A Method name can contain any number of words without spaces.
Recommended to start word first letter as lowercase
If method name contains multiple words then recommended to write from second word onwords every first character in Uppercase
eg: saveUserAll();
4. Naming conventions for the Constants:
----------------------------------------
constant means fixed value.
Recommended to write constant variable all character in uppercase.
If constant variable contains multiple words, recommendes to use _(underscore) with all uppercase character.
eg: int MIN_AGE =21;
    final int MIN_AGE = 21; //final used to represent this as constant variable, and they can't be changed in future.
Note: Reinitializing is not accepted for constant, it will throw error.
5. Naming conventions for the Constants:
----------------------------------------
package name can have any number of characters and any no of words
Recommended to use only lowercase letter in package names.
If package name contains multiple words, we will use .(dot) to seperate  words
eg: java.lang, com.alchemist
Note: classname and interface name conventions are same.
      Java naming conventions are also known as Java code standard.
	  Variable name and method naming conventions also called as camel case format.
	  
