/*=========================================================
STATIC BLOCK VS INSTANCE BLOCK
=========================================================*/
STATIC BLOCK
------------
1. Executes when class loads.
2. Executes only once.
3. Executes before main().
4. Used for class initialization.

INSTANCE BLOCK
--------------
1. Executes during object creation.
2. Executes every object creation.
3. Executes before constructor.
4. Used for object initialization.

Note: 1. When we run java program JVM will check for static members ie static variables, static methods, static block(JVM will allocate memory to them
         in same sequence). Once memory allocated for static members, then it will start execution in order as Static block, static method(if we call
	     ie only main() will execute automatically by JVM), static variable. This is static control flow.
	  2. Non-static fields cannot be accessed in static area. For accessing non-static variable we need to create object and then we can access instance
	     variable into static area.
	  3. Instance controll flow will begin when object is created, memory will be allocated for instance variable, instance methods and instance blocks.
	     Once memory allocation completed then, execution will happen in order like Instace block, constructor, instance method (If we call)
	  4. Static members can be acceessed directly in instance areas because for static members, memory already allocated at the time of class loading.
	     Static variables can be accessed directly in static block.

ex:
public class ControlFlowDemo {

    // Static Variable
    static int a = initializeStaticVariable();

    // Static Block 1
    static {
        System.out.println("Static Block 1");
    }

    // Static Block 2
    static {
        System.out.println("Static Block 2");
    }

    // Instance Variable
    int b = initializeInstanceVariable();

    // Instance Block 1
    {
        System.out.println("Instance Block 1");
    }

    // Instance Block 2
    {
        System.out.println("Instance Block 2");
    }

    // Constructor
    public ControlFlowDemo() {
        System.out.println("Constructor");
    }

    // Static Method
    static void staticMethod() {
        System.out.println("Static Method");

        // Cannot directly access non-static variable
        // System.out.println(b); // Compile Error

        ControlFlowDemo obj = new ControlFlowDemo();
        System.out.println("Accessing Instance Variable in Static Method: " + obj.b);
    }

    // Instance Method
    void instanceMethod() {
        System.out.println("Instance Method");
    }

    static int initializeStaticVariable() {
        System.out.println("Static Variable Initialization");
        return 10;
    }

    int initializeInstanceVariable() {
        System.out.println("Instance Variable Initialization");
        return 20;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        System.out.println("Main Method Started");

        staticMethod();

        System.out.println("\nCreating Object...");

        ControlFlowDemo obj = new ControlFlowDemo();

        obj.instanceMethod();

        System.out.println("Main Method Ended");
    }
}

