## 1. Can We Start a Thread Multiple Times?

No. We cannot start the same Thread object more than once.

### Example

```java
public class Demo extends Thread {

    @Override
    public void run() {
        System.out.println("Thread is executing");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Demo d = new Demo();

        d.start();
        d.start(); // Illegal
    }
}
```

### Output

The first `start()` call starts the thread.

The second `start()` call throws:

```text
java.lang.IllegalThreadStateException
```

### Important points

- A Thread object can be started only once.
- After a thread terminates, it cannot be restarted.
- If we need to execute the same task again, create a new Thread object or submit the task again to an ExecutorService.

Example:

```java
Demo d1 = new Demo();
Demo d2 = new Demo();

d1.start();
d2.start();
```

Both are separate Thread objects.

