============================================================
10. IMPORTANT POINT ABOUT ARRAYLIST
============================================================

ArrayList is not recommended when frequent insertions
and deletions are required in the middle of a large list.

Reason:
-------

- Elements may need to be shifted during insertion
  or deletion.
- This can affect performance.

ArrayList is suitable when:
---------------------------

- Frequent retrieval is required.
- Index-based access is required.
- Insertion and deletion at the end are common.

LinkedList can be considered when frequent insertions
and deletions are required, depending on the access pattern.


