               CUSTOM OBJECT IN ARRAYLIST
============================================================

We can store user-defined class objects inside ArrayList.

Example:

public class Student {

    int id;
    String name;

    public Student(int id, String name) {

        this.id = id;
        this.name = name;

    }

    @Override
    public String toString() {

